+      "summary": "A listening companion that turns anything spoken into live context pages. It listens to speech from a television, a live event, a browser or a meeting, transcribes what is said, works out which topics are worth noting, researches them instantly, and builds a presentation page per topic with summarised key information, sources, and a fitting background image. Every page joins a chronological timeline, so a session can be scrolled back through afterwards. First showcase is political debates, where viewers can see how far a claim sits from verified information, but it is a general tool for meetings, events, and conversation. Research stage: transcription, claim detection, and search pieces are all borrowed from existing services; the build is the salience judgement, the page presentation, and the timeline.",
