+      "jumpstartPrompt": "You are helping O'keito S. (Melbourne) scope Karen's Hotline.\n\n## Product thesis\nA web experience where an animated character named Karen (AI voice) listens to consumer complaints about any company or service. The AI structures the complaint, stores it, and can notify the brand with a discreet remedy opportunity. Consumers vent safely and may receive a voucher or special (from that brand or another industry brand that opted in). Brands reduce public bad reviews, offload stressful call scenarios from support staff, and can advertise by funding specials for relevant complainants.\n\n## Actors\n1. Consumer (venter): talks to Karen, feels heard, optional offer at the end.\n2. Brand (client): receives structured complaint briefs, can remedy privately, can sponsor offers.\n3. Operator (O / MarvelUs-style): runs the page, AI pipeline, brand outreach, offer marketplace.\n\n## Core loops\n1. Consumer opens page, talks or types to animated Karen, AI extracts company, issue, desired outcome, contact opt-in, then confirmation.\n2. Backend stores complaint; if brand is a client (or outreach list), send discreet brief + remedy CTA.\n3. Brand remedies or issues voucher; consumer gets follow-up.\n4. Non-client brands get a sales outreach: join to intercept complaints and offer specials (ad model).\n\n## Non-goals (phase 0)\n- Not a fake review farm. Never post or suppress reviews on Google/Yelp on behalf of brands without clear lawful process.\n- Not a substitute for emergency services or legal advice.\n- Do not harass brands with spam; consent and opt-in for ongoing leads.\n- Do not deepfake a real person named Karen without rights; use an original animated character.\n\n## Phase plan\n### Phase 0: Vent MVP (consumer only)\nLanding page + animated Karen avatar (simple) + voice and/or text chat (Realtime or STT+LLM). Structured complaint form fields filled by AI. Store to DB/sheet. Email O on each complaint. No brand sends yet.\nExit: 10 test vents recorded with structured JSON.\n\n### Phase 1: Brand brief + remedy\nPDF/email brief template to brands. Manual send first. Track remedy / ignore / voucher. Legal/privacy copy for consumers and brands.\n\n### Phase 2: Offer marketplace\nBrand portal: opt in, set offer rules (category, geography, max redemptions). When a matching complaint arrives, Karen can present the offer after venting.\n\n### Phase 3: Scale and compliance\nAuto brand matching, billing for leads or subscriptions, abuse detection, AU spam/privacy compliance.\n\n## Monetization (hypotheses)\n- SaaS / per-complaint lead fee to brands\n- Sponsored offers (ad inventory after vent)\n- Premium brand dashboard\n\n## Deliverables for this jumpstart\n1. One-sentence thesis and ethics boundaries.\n2. Complaint schema (fields the AI must capture).\n3. Consumer page UX outline (calm vent, not rage-bait).\n4. Brand outreach email draft (dash-free).\n5. Phase 0 tech sketch (web avatar + voice + store).\n6. Risks: defamation, consent, impersonation, review-platform ToS, support-desk politics.\n7. Open questions for O (AU-only first?, categories, free vent vs gated).\n\nWrite dash-free copy. Practical over hype."
