+      "jumpstartPrompt": "You are helping O'keito S. (Melbourne) ship a tiny Job Board MVP.\n\n## Product\nPut up a big QR code poster that asks: Do you need help with any local job? When someone scans, they get a simple mobile form to submit a local job request with: what the job entails, date, time, duration, money offered, and contact details. Phase 0 is demand capture only (poster + form + inbox). Matching helpers comes later.\n\n## Non-goals (phase 0)\n- No full two-sided marketplace app yet.\n- No payments processing yet.\n- No worker app yet.\n- Do not overbuild auth.\n\n## Phase plan\n### Phase 0: Poster + form\n1. One landing page with clear headline and short trust line (Melbourne local help requests).\n2. Form fields: job title/summary, details/entail, preferred date, time window, duration estimate, budget/offer amount, suburb, name, phone or email, optional photos later.\n3. Submit to email and/or Formspree/sheet/HighLevel; confirmation message on success.\n4. Print-ready A3/A2 poster with huge QR, short copy, no clutter.\n5. Privacy one-liner on the form.\n\nExit: live URL + printable PDF/PNG poster + one test submission received.\n\n### Phase 1: Triage inbox\nSimple list of submissions (sheet or tiny admin). Tag: new / contacted / filled / spam. Optional auto-SMS or email to O on new lead.\n\n### Phase 2: Soft match\nForward vetted jobs to known helpers or a small helper waitlist. Still manual matching.\n\n### Phase 3: Light marketplace (only if demand is real)\nHelper signup, job browse, accept flow. Still Melbourne suburbs first.\n\n## Deliverables for this jumpstart\n1. One-sentence thesis.\n2. Exact form field list and validation rules.\n3. Poster copy (dash-free) and layout notes.\n4. Tech pick for phase 0 (e.g. GitHub Pages + Formspree, or Cloudflare + form).\n5. Spam/abuse risks and mitigations.\n6. Week-1 ship checklist.\n7. Open questions for O (where posters go, paid vs free posts, categories).\n\nWrite dash-free copy. Keep it practical and Melbourne-first."
