+        "saas",
+        "kids",
+        "math",
+        "modules"
+      ],
+      "jumpstartPrompt": "You are building a native Mac product for parents. Working name: Parent School Lock (rename later).\n\n## Vision\nA Mac menu bar app (plus browser extension) that parents install on the family Mac their child uses. During school hours or any parent-chosen windows, distracting apps and sites are hard-blocked. Instead of an empty lock screen, the child sees a calm lesson player that runs modular school content (Math Module Pack v1 first). Modules are downloadable and swappable so we can ship Reading, Science, etc. later without rewriting the shell.\n\nThis is inspired by personal forced time boxing blockers (schedule + blocklist + accountability password on Mac + Chrome), but pivoted for families:\n- Parent holds the bypass (PIN / remote unlock). Child never holds full unlock power.\n- Blocked state is the product surface (lessons), not just a deny page.\n- Allowlists for school tools matter as much as blocklists.\n- Trust, notarization, clear permissions, and tamper resistance beat vibe-coded novelty.\n\n## Non-goals (Phase 0 to 2)\n- Do not build iOS/iPad yet.\n- Do not claim Apple Screen Time / Family Controls parity on day one (document the escalation path).\n- Do not scrape or sync raw kid browsing history to a cloud by default.\n- Do not sell pay-to-unlock distractions as the core monetization. Sell curriculum packs, multi-child seats, and parent reports later.\n- Do not invent curriculum that pretends to be an official school board syllabus. Ship clear practice modules with grade bands.\n\n## Users and roles\n1. Parent (admin): schedules, block/allow lists, PIN, module downloads, progress view, one-tap exceptions (sick day / half day).\n2. Child (supervised): during lock windows, can only use allowlisted apps/sites + the in-app lesson player. Cannot change schedule or disable blocking without parent PIN.\n3. Optional co-parent (Phase 2+): second admin with shared policy.\n\n## Core product loops\n1. Parent setup: install Mac app, grant permissions, install Chrome (later Safari) extension, pick School Day preset, review distraction categories, set parent PIN, download Math Module Pack v1, assign grade band.\n2. School window: schedule flips to LOCKED, blocked apps/sites refuse open, menu bar shows lock, lesson hub is the productive surface.\n3. Lesson: child completes short modular units (explain, practice, check). Progress saved locally; parent can see completion.\n4. Exception: parent unlocks with PIN for N minutes or until end of day without deleting the standing weekly schedule.\n5. After hours: FREE PLAY or softer mode per schedule; lessons still available on demand.\n\n## Architecture (must live on the Mac)\nA website cannot force-quit local apps. Build:\nA) macOS menu bar app (Swift / SwiftUI preferred; Electron only if you justify MVP tradeoffs and document notarization risks).\nB) Browser extension (Chrome MV3 first) for site blocking + allowlist.\nC) Local module store (on-disk packages: manifest + content + assets).\nD) Optional lightweight sync later. Phase 0 is local-first.\n\n### Enforcement honesty (required in README)\n- Tier A (MVP): menu bar agent + extension block pages + best-effort app restrict. Bypassable by savvy kids.\n- Tier B: Safari extension + broader monitoring + uninstall protection requiring PIN.\n- Tier C (roadmap): Screen Time / FamilyControls / MDM-class. Do not fake Tier C in marketing.\n\n## Phase plan (stop and demo after each)\n\n### Phase 0: Product skeleton (1 to 2 days)\nMenu bar Locked / Unlocked / Exception. Parent Settings (PIN gated) with weekly schedule (default Mon to Fri 8:30 to 15:30). One-tap exceptions. Local store for schedule, PIN hash, child profile. Demo mode without real blocking.\nExit: schedule + PIN work; README states Tier A limits.\n\n### Phase 1: Blocking MVP\nChrome blocklist by category (Social, Video, Games, Chat) with starter domains. School allowlist (Classroom, Docs, Drive, Khan Academy, lesson origin). Mac app bundle restrictions when LOCKED. Parent wizard with category presets (not cloud-synced raw history). Browser interstitial with Open today's math lesson deep link.\nExit: LOCKED blocks listed sites; allowlist works; PIN unlocks; schedule flips in seconds.\n\n### Phase 2: Lesson shell + Math Module Pack v1\nLesson Hub (engaging kid skin, calm parent settings). Module format via module.json + offline lessons. Math packs for Years 3 to 4 and 5 to 6 (number sense, fractions intro, times tables, word problems). Original practice content only. Progress tab for parent. Optional earn 10 min browse after 1 lesson toggle, off by default.\nExit: install math pack, complete a lesson offline, parent sees progress.\n\n### Phase 3: Module catalog plumbing\nRemote catalog JSON, download + checksum, install to Application Support, update modules without full app update, packager script. Stubs for Reading, Science, Touch typing.\nExit: second stub module installs cleanly.\n\n### Phase 4: Family trust + distribution\nNotarized build path, update mechanism, Chrome Web Store notes, Safari scaffold, co-parent + unlock audit log, privacy docs, waitlist landing outline. Stripe hooks for packs later.\nExit: signed build docs + privacy README + waitlist outline.\n\n### Phase 5: Hardening roadmap (design unless time)\nBypass metrics, optional DNS, iPad note, FamilyControls feasibility memo.\n\n## UX principles\nParent UI: calm, light mode, plain permissions. Kid UI: focused, large targets, no shame. Empty lock screens are a failure. Always offer the next lesson. Never use em dashes in user-facing copy.\n\n## Repo layout\n/apps/mac-menubar\n/apps/chrome-extension\n/packages/module-schema\n/modules/math-y3-y4\n/modules/math-y5-y6\n/docs/ENFORCEMENT-TIERS.md\n/docs/MODULE-FORMAT.md\n/docs/PRIVACY.md\n/catalog/catalog.json\n\n## First build loop\n1. Scaffold menu bar + settings + schedule + PIN + demo lock\n2. Scaffold Chrome block/allow + interstitial\n3. Wire LOCKED to both\n4. Lesson Hub + one sample lesson\n5. Module loader + Math v1\n6. ENFORCEMENT-TIERS.md\n7. 5-minute parent demo script\n\n## Acceptance demo\nParent sets Mon to Fri 9:00 to 15:00 LOCKED. Child opens YouTube, gets interstitial, opens lesson, completes one math lesson, parent sees progress. Parent grants 15 minute exception, YouTube works, exception ends, blocked again. Weekly schedule still intact.\n\nStart at Phase 0 now. After each phase, summarize what works, what is still bypassable, and what parents should not expect yet.\n\n## Done when\n- New idea is first in data/ideas.json\n- JSON validates\n- PR opened (merged if allowed)\n- Report live URL https://marvelus-tech.github.io/project-ideas/\n- Confirm card title Parent School Lock (Mac app + lessons) will show after Pages rebuild\n\nDo not invent extra ideas. Do not rewrite other entries."
