+      "jumpstartPrompt": "You are an AI coding and product agent. Your task is to jumpstart validation and MVP planning for a kids learning games app targeting the App Store subscription market.\n\n## Research Phase\n\n1. **Identify comps**: Research and list 5-10 successful kids educational apps on the iOS App Store currently generating significant revenue through weekly subscriptions ($5-$10/week range). Focus on apps with extensive onboarding flows (20+ screens).\n\n2. **App Store monetization research**: Analyze pricing strategies, trial periods (if any), subscription tiers, and estimated revenue for the identified comps. Document what subscription models perform best in the kids education category.\n\n3. **Onboarding clone analysis**: For the top 3 performing apps, document their onboarding structure: number of screens, permission requests, value propositions per screen, parent gate implementations, and conversion tactics. Create a flow diagram for each.\n\n4. **COPPA and kids privacy compliance**: Document all US COPPA requirements and Apple App Store requirements for kids category apps. Include: required privacy policy elements, parental consent mechanisms, data collection restrictions, and third-party service limitations.\n\n5. **Melbourne/US distribution angle**: Research requirements for publishing from Melbourne to US App Store, including: business entity needs, tax implications (W-8BEN form), payment processing, and any geo-specific compliance requirements.\n\n## MVP Planning Phase\n\n6. **2-week MVP scope**: Design a minimal but shippable kids learning app focused on one subject area (suggest: early math or phonics). Specify:\n   - Core learning mechanic (3-5 game types max)\n   - Content scope (how many lessons/levels for initial launch)\n   - 25-30 onboarding screens structure with specific purposes\n   - Basic progress tracking for parents\n   - Subscription paywall placement and messaging\n   - Tech stack recommendation (React Native vs Swift vs Flutter)\n   - Asset creation plan (illustrations, animations, sounds)\n\n7. **Week-by-week breakdown**: Provide a detailed 2-week sprint plan showing what gets built each day to hit an MVP that can be submitted to App Store review.\n\n## Deliverables\n\nProvide a comprehensive markdown document with:\n- Comp analysis table\n- Monetization strategy recommendation\n- Complete onboarding flow mockup (screen-by-screen outline)\n- COPPA compliance checklist\n- Distribution setup guide\n- Detailed 2-week build plan\n- Risk factors and mitigation strategies\n\nFocus on practical, actionable guidance that can be immediately executed by a solo developer or small team in Melbourne targeting the US market."
