+      "jumpstartPrompt": "Build a remote MCP server that provides daily quotes and rituals for AI agent morning briefings.\n\n## Core Tools\n\n1. **get_quote** - Returns a curated quote with metadata:\n   - Input: optional theme (motivation/wisdom/creativity/focus)\n   - Output: quote text, author, source, theme tags, quote ID\n   - Behavior: tracks previously served quotes per connection to avoid repeats\n\n2. **get_todays_ritual** - Returns structured morning ritual:\n   - Output: quote, 3 focus areas for the day, brief reflection prompt\n   - Uses quote://today resource URI pattern\n\n3. **set_theme_preference** - Store user's preferred quote themes:\n   - Input: array of preferred themes\n   - Persists across sessions per OAuth user\n\n4. **get_quote_history** - Recent quotes served to this user (last 30 days)\n\n## OAuth and State\n\n- OAuth 2.0 with scopes: `quotes:read`, `preferences:write`\n- Per-user state tracking: served quote IDs, theme preferences, streak count\n- Standing rule integration: agent can auto-fetch quote://today every morning\n\n## Data and Content\n\n- Seed database: 500+ quotes across 5 themes\n- Quote schema: id, text, author, source, themes[], addedDate\n- Smart rotation: no repeat within 90 days per user\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- MCP server deployed and connectable via mcp.json config\n- OAuth flow works in Cursor/Claude Desktop\n- get_quote returns different quotes on successive calls\n- quote://today resource works in agent context\n- Light-themed documentation site with connection instructions\n\n## Tech Stack\n\n- Cloudflare Workers + Durable Objects for state\n- OAuth via Workers OAuth library\n- Quote storage in D1 or KV\n- MCP SDK for tool definitions\n\nDeliver: working MCP server URL, example mcp.json config, 10-quote demo script, and connection guide."
