+      "jumpstartPrompt": "Build a remote MCP server for a local cafe/restaurant with menu browsing, wait time checks, and pickup orders.\n\n## Core Tools\n\n1. **get_menu** - Retrieve current menu:\n   - Output: categories (drinks, food, pastries), items with name, description, price, dietary tags, availability\n   - Include daily specials\n\n2. **check_wait_time** - Current pickup wait estimate:\n   - Output: estimated minutes, current order queue length, kitchen status\n\n3. **place_pickup_order** - Submit order for pickup:\n   - Input: items array (itemId, quantity, modifications), pickup name, pickup time preference\n   - Output: order ID, estimated ready time, total price\n\n4. **simulate_payment** - Complete simulated payment:\n   - Input: orderId, paymentMethod (fake)\n   - Output: confirmation, pickup instructions\n\n5. **get_order_status** - Check order progress:\n   - Output: status (received/preparing/ready), updated ready time\n\n6. **get_usual_order** - Retrieve user's frequent order (OAuth):\n   - Requires `orders:history` scope\n   - Returns most common order for quick reorder\n\n## Features\n\n- Standing rules support: agent can auto-check usual order availability\n- Host triggers: owner can set 'new daily special' trigger\n- Order modifications: extra shot, oat milk, no ice, etc.\n- Melbourne cafe vibe: flat white, batch brew, sourdough options\n\n## OAuth and State\n\n- Scopes: `menu:read`, `orders:write`, `orders:history`\n- Per-user order history (last 90 days)\n- Usual order detection algorithm\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- Agent can browse menu and place order\n- Wait time accurately reflects queue\n- Usual order shortcut works for repeat customers\n- Clear pickup instructions in confirmation\n- Light-themed menu display\n\n## Tech Stack\n\n- Cloudflare Workers MCP server\n- D1 for menu and order history\n- Durable Object for real-time queue management\n- Simple admin UI for cafe owner to update menu\n\nDeliver: working MCP server, sample menu with 30+ items, demo script showing usual order flow, connection guide."
