+      "jumpstartPrompt": "Build a remote MCP server for freelance studio/agency client intake and scoping workflow.\n\n## Core Tools\n\n1. **create_lead** - Start new lead:\n   - Input: contact name, email, project type, initial description\n   - Output: lead ID, next steps\n   - Triggers owner notification\n\n2. **ask_discovery_questions** - Agent-guided elicitation:\n   - System provides contextual questions based on project type\n   - Covers: budget range, timeline, must-haves vs nice-to-haves, decision makers\n   - Agent asks questions naturally in conversation\n\n3. **propose_scope** - Draft scope document:\n   - Input: lead ID, gathered requirements\n   - Output: structured scope with phases, deliverables, exclusions\n   - Requires owner approval before sending\n\n4. **send_estimate** - Generate and send estimate:\n   - Input: lead ID, hours per phase, hourly rate\n   - Output: formatted estimate PDF, validity period\n   - Logged in owner's review queue\n\n5. **book_call** - Schedule discovery call:\n   - Integration with calendar (or simulated availability)\n   - Input: preferred times from lead\n   - Output: confirmed meeting link\n\n6. **get_intake_queue** - Owner's pending approvals:\n   - Returns leads needing scope review or estimate approval\n   - Not a raw CRM dump; filtered actionable queue\n\n## Intelligence Layer\n\n- Smart question selection based on project type (web dev vs branding vs ongoing retainer)\n- Budget qualification without being pushy\n- Red flag detection (unrealistic timeline, scope creep signals)\n- Automatic scope template selection\n\n## OAuth and Permissions\n\n- Scopes: `leads:write`, `estimates:write`, `calendar:read`\n- Owner role: approve scopes and estimates before send\n- Agent role: conduct intake, draft documents\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- Agent can conduct natural intake conversation\n- Discovery questions adapt to project type\n- Scope and estimate require owner approval (no auto-send)\n- Owner queue shows only actionable items\n- Light-themed estimate templates\n\n## Tech Stack\n\n- Cloudflare Workers MCP server\n- D1 for leads and project data\n- Durable Object for real-time intake sessions\n- PDF generation for estimates (cloudflare-workers-pdf or similar)\n\nDeliver: MCP server, 3 project type templates (web build, branding, retainer), intake conversation demo script, owner approval workflow guide."
