+      "jumpstartPrompt": "Build a remote MCP server for event ticketing with seat holds and simulated purchases.\n\n## Core Tools\n\n1. **search_events** - Browse upcoming events:\n   - Input: location, date range, category (music, sports, theater)\n   - Output: events with date, venue, price range, availability\n\n2. **get_event_details** - Full event info:\n   - Input: event ID\n   - Output: description, venue map, seating chart, ticket tiers, terms\n\n3. **hold_seats** - Reserve seats temporarily:\n   - Input: event ID, section, quantity\n   - Output: hold ID, seats assigned, hold expires at (10 minutes)\n   - Removes seats from availability for other agents\n\n4. **get_hold_timer** - Check remaining hold time:\n   - Input: hold ID\n   - Output: seconds remaining, seats held\n\n5. **simulate_purchase** - Complete simulated buy:\n   - Input: hold ID\n   - Output: simulated confirmation, ticket IDs, QR codes (fake)\n   - SIMULATED PURCHASE badge displayed\n   - Never charges real money\n\n6. **release_hold** - Cancel seat hold:\n   - Input: hold ID\n   - Returns seats to availability\n   - Auto-releases after 10 minute timeout\n\n7. **get_my_tickets** - View purchased tickets:\n   - Output: upcoming events with ticket details\n\n## Hold Timer System\n\n- Seats held for 10 minutes to prevent competition issues\n- Timer displayed in all responses while hold active\n- Auto-release after expiration (Durable Object alarm)\n- Other agents see held seats as unavailable\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- Agent can search events and hold seats\n- Hold timer prevents seat conflicts\n- Auto-release works after 10 minutes\n- Simulated purchase clearly marked (no real charges)\n- Seating chart visualization (simple ASCII or JSON)\n- Light-themed event listings\n\n## Tech Stack\n\n- Cloudflare Workers MCP server\n- Durable Object for seat inventory and hold state\n- Alarm API for auto-release\n- D1 for event catalog\n- Simulated QR code generation\n\nDeliver: MCP server, 50+ demo even