+      "savedAt": "2026-09-06",
+      "source": "https://marvelus-tech.github.io/project-ideas/",
+      "sourceLabel": "Remote MCP and WebMCP notes",
+      "summary": "First-class Connections, Standing jobs, Hands (may-run vs must-ask); initiative is policy not protocol.",
+      "tags": [
+        "remote-mcp",
+        "ai-agent",
+        "automation",
+        "personal-assistant"
+      ],
+      "jumpstartPrompt": "Design and build a personal AI agent platform with first-class support for connections, standing jobs, and permission levels.\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n**Connections**: MCP servers the agent can access\n- User adds connections via OAuth in settings UI\n- Each connection has scopes and permission level\n\n**Standing Jobs**: recurring tasks agent should handle automatically\n- Examples: morning brief, inbox triage, expense tracking\n- User configures job schedule and requirements\n- Agent executes without prompting\n\n**Hands** (permission levels):\n- **May-run**: agent can execute without asking (e.g., check calendar, read emails)\n- **Must-ask**: agent drafts action and waits for approval (e.g., send email, make purchase)\n- Per-connection and per-tool granularity\n\n**Initiative as Policy**: agent proactively suggests tasks based on:  \n- Standing job definitions  \n- Calendar events  \n- Detected patterns  \n- User-configured rules  \n\n## Platform Features\n\n1. **Connection Manager**:\n   - Add/remove MCP servers\n   - Configure OAuth per connection\n   - Set permission level (may-run / must-ask) per tool\n\n2. **Standing Jobs Dashboard**:\n   - Create job (name, schedule, connected tools, success criteria)\n   - View job history and outcomes\n   - Adjust frequency and parameters\n\n3. **Approval Queue**:\n   - Pending must-ask actions\n   - One-click approve/deny\n   - Bulk actions for routine approvals\n\n4. **Agent Logs**:\n   - What agent did automatically (may-run)\n   - What agent asked about (must-ask)\n   - Tool call history per connection\n\n## Example Standing Jobs\n\n- **Morning Brief**: 7am daily; get_quote, check_calendar (next 24h), check_email (unread count), check_weather; compile into brief message\n- **Expense Tracker**: daily; scan transactions for business expenses, categorize, draft monthly report\n- **Inbox Triage**: every 2 hours; check_inbox, flag urgent emails, draft replies for must-ask approval\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- User can add MCP connections and set permission levels\n- Standing jobs execute on schedule without manual triggers\n- Agent proactively suggests new standing jobs based on usage patterns\n- Must-ask actions wait in approval queue; may-run actions just happen\n- Light-themed dashboard for managing connections and jobs\n- Clear audit log of all agent actions\n\n## Tech Stack\n\n- Next.js web app for user dashboard\n- Cloudflare Workers for agent runtime\n- Durable Objects for agent state and job scheduling\n- D1 for user config, connections, and job definitions\n- OAuth proxy for MCP connections\n- Cron Triggers for standing job execution\n\n## Deliverables\n\nBuild:\n- User dashboard (connection manager, standing jobs, approval queue)\n- Agent runtime with may-run/must-ask enforcement\n- 3 demo standing jobs configured\n- Connection to 3 demo MCP servers (quotes, calendar, email)\n- Permission policy engine\n- Job scheduling system\n\nProvide: architecture diagram, permission model documentation, standing job template guide, demo walkthrough video."
