+      "jumpstartPrompt": "Build a WebMCP demo store showing two paths to the same goal: DOM manipulation vs remote MCP tools.\n\n## Concept\n\nSingle product page with two ways to shop:\n\n**Path A (WebMCP DOM tools)**: Agent clicks buttons, fills forms, uses page UI like a human\n- Tools: click, type, scroll, read DOM\n- Simulates visitor interaction\n\n**Path B (Remote MCP tools)**: Agent uses structured data APIs\n- Tools: search_products, get_product, add_to_cart, get_cart, checkout\n- Simulates backend integration\n\n**Comparison**: both paths complete same task; show time and tool calls for each\n\n## Page Design\n\n- Product grid (20 items with images, names, prices)\n- Search bar\n- Add to cart buttons\n- Cart sidebar\n- Checkout form\n- Light theme, clean layout\n\n## Remote MCP Tools\n\n1. **search_products** - Find products:\n   - Input: query string\n   - Output: matching products with IDs\n\n2. **get_product** - Product details:\n   - Input: product ID\n   - Output: name, price, description, inStock\n\n3. **add_to_cart** - Add item:\n   - Input: product ID, quantity\n   - Output: updated cart\n\n4. **get_cart** - Current cart\n\n5. **apply_coupon** - Discount code:\n   - Remote MCP holds coupon logic (not in page HTML)\n\n6. **checkout** - Complete purchase (simulated)\n\n## Demo Script\n\nTask: \"Buy 2 blue t-shirts and apply coupon SAVE10\"\n\n- Agent A: uses WebMCP to search, click products, fill cart, enter coupon, checkout\n- Agent B: uses remote MCP search_products, add_to_cart, apply_coupon, checkout\n- Display: side-by-side tool call counts, elapsed time\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- Both paths successfully complete purchase\n- Tool call comparison shows structured APIs are faster\n- Coupon logic hidden in remote MCP (not scrapeable from page)\n- Page works for both WebMCP and remote MCP simultaneously\n- Light-themed product page\n- Clear visual indicator of which path agent is using\n\n## Tech Stack\n\n- Static HTML page with product grid (WebMCP target)\n- JavaScript for cart interactions\n- Cloudflare Workers MCP server for remote tools\n- Side-by-side demo dashboard showing both agents\n\nDeliver: product page, remote MCP server, demo script showing both paths, comparison metrics dashboard."
