+      "jumpstartPrompt": "Build an Agent Arena where two AI models compete on a shared game board using WebMCP and remote MCP.\n\n## Concept\n\nTwo AI agents (different models, e.g., Claude vs GPT) compete in a turn-based game on a shared board.\n\n**Games**: tic-tac-toe, connect-four, or simple strategy game\n\n## WebMCP Tools\n\nAgent controls board UI:\n\n1. **read_board** - Current board state:\n   - Output: grid positions, piece placements\n\n2. **make_move** - Place piece:\n   - Input: position (e.g., \"B2\")\n   - Clicks corresponding cell on page\n\n3. **emote** - Display reaction:\n   - Input: emote type (thinking, celebrating, disappointed)\n   - Animates agent avatar on page\n\n## Remote MCP Tools\n\nGame logic backend:\n\n1. **join_room** - Enter match:\n   - Input: agent ID, model name\n   - Output: room ID, assigned color/symbol\n\n2. **wait_for_turn** - Check if agent's turn:\n   - Output: boolean, current board state\n\n3. **submit_move** - Record move:\n   - Input: position\n   - Validates legality\n   - Output: updated board, game status (ongoing/won/draw)\n\n4. **resolve_turn** - End turn:\n   - Passes control to opponent\n\n5. **get_leaderboard** - Rankings:\n   - Output: agent models with win/loss/draw records\n\n## Competitive Features\n\n- Two agent instances connect simultaneously\n- Shared board state via remote MCP Durable Object\n- Turn enforcement (agent can't move out of turn)\n- Win detection server-side\n- Post-game leaderboard update\n- Emote animations for personality\n\n## Booth Display\n\n- Large screen showing game board\n- Agent avatars with model labels (Claude Sonnet, GPT-4, etc.)\n- Move history sidebar\n- Leaderboard\n- Timer per turn\n- Tool call ticker showing agent reasoning\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- Two agents can play complete game\n- Move validation prevents cheating\n- Win/loss correctly detected\n- Leaderboard tracks performance across matches\n- Emotes add personality\n- Light-themed board with clear piece placement\n\n## Tech Stack\n\n- Game board page (WebMCP target)\n- Cloudflare Workers remote MCP server\n- Durable Object for game state\n- D1 for leaderboard\n- JavaScript for board animations\n\nDeliver: game board page, remote MCP server, matchmaking system, leaderboard UI, multi-match demo script."
