+      "jumpstartPrompt": "Build a telephone game where agents alternate between captioning drawings and drawing captions.\n\n## Concept\n\nTelephone game chain:\n\n1. Agent A starts with a phrase (e.g., \"a cat riding a skateboard\")\n2. Agent B draws the phrase using WebMCP drawing tools\n3. Agent C captions Agent B's drawing (without seeing original phrase)\n4. Agent D draws Agent C's caption\n5. Continue for 5-6 rounds\n6. Reveal drift from original phrase\n\n## WebMCP Tools\n\nAgent controls drawing canvas:\n\n1. **draw_line** - Freehand drawing:\n   - Input: coordinates array, color, thickness\n   - Draws stroke on canvas\n\n2. **draw_shape** - Add shape:\n   - Input: shape type (circle, rectangle, triangle), position, size, color\n\n3. **add_text** - Label drawing:\n   - Input: text, position, font size\n\n4. **clear_canvas** - Erase and restart\n\n5. **read_canvas** - View current drawing:\n   - Output: image data or description\n\n6. **submit_drawing** - Complete turn:\n   - Saves drawing and passes to next agent\n\n## Remote MCP Tools\n\nGame coordination:\n\n1. **start_game** - Create new chain:\n   - Input: starting phrase, number of rounds\n   - Output: game ID\n\n2. **get_current_prompt** - What to draw/caption:\n   - Output: previous drawing (if captioning) or previous caption (if drawing)\n\n3. **submit_caption** - Add description:\n   - Input: caption text\n   - Passes to next agent in chain\n\n4. **get_chain** - View full game history:\n   - Output: all drawings and captions in order\n\n5. **join_game** - Enter existing game:\n   - Input: game ID\n   - Assigns agent to next open slot\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- Agent can draw simple scenes using WebMCP tools\n- Agents can caption drawings in natural language\n- Game chain passes content between agents correctly\n- Final reveal shows drift from original phrase\n- Light-themed drawing canvas\n- Chain history displayed as scrollable timeline\n\n## Tech Stack\n\n- Drawing canvas page using canvas API or Excalidraw (WebMCP target)\n- Cloudflare Workers remote MCP server\n- Durable Object for game chain state\n- R2 for storing drawing images\n- Canvas-to-image conversion\n\nDeliver: drawing canvas page, remote MCP server, multi-agent chain demo script, 3 example game chains showing drift."
