+      "jumpstartPrompt": "Build the simplest possible WebMCP + remote MCP booth game: Hot Potato. Fast rounds, minimal code, maximum demo value.\n\n## Concept\n\nMulti-agent hot potato game. Agents pass a potato, timer counts down, agent holding potato when timer hits zero loses.\n\n**Target**: under 1 minute rounds, shippable in one week.\n\n## WebMCP Tools\n\nAgent controls board UI:\n\n1. **read_board** - See current state:\n   - Output: who has potato, timer remaining, other agents in game\n\n2. **pass_potato** - Send to another agent:\n   - Input: target agent ID\n   - Clicks agent avatar on page\n\n3. **taunt** - Display message:\n   - Input: taunt text\n   - Animates speech bubble\n\n## Remote MCP Tools\n\nGame coordination:\n\n1. **create_match** - Start new game:\n   - Input: round duration (30-60 seconds)\n   - Output: match ID\n\n2. **join_match** - Enter game:\n   - Input: match ID\n   - Output: agent's position, other players\n\n3. **place_potato** - Pass potato:\n   - Input: target agent ID\n   - Server validates (can't pass to self, must have potato)\n   - Output: success, updated board state\n\n4. **get_scores** - Round results:\n   - Output: loser (who held potato at timeout), winners\n\n5. **get_leaderboard** - Win/loss records:\n   - All agents sorted by win rate\n\n## Game Flow\n\n1. 3-4 agents join match\n2. Random agent starts with potato\n3. Timer starts (45 seconds)\n4. Agents pass potato rapidly\n5. Timer hits zero\n6. Agent holding potato loses\n7. Scores updated\n8. Next round\n\n## Booth Display\n\n- Large screen with agent avatars in circle\n- Potato icon moves between avatars\n- Countdown timer prominent\n- Taunt speech bubbles for personality\n- Light theme\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- 3+ agents can play simultaneously\n- Potato passing works via WebMCP or remote MCP\n- Timer accurate, server-authoritative\n- Loser correctly identified\n- Fast rounds keep booth visitors engaged\n- Minimal code (shippable in 1 week)\n\n## Tech Stack\n\n- Simple board page (WebMCP target)\n- Cloudflare Workers remote MCP server\n- Durable Object for match state and timer\n- Alarm API for timeout enforcement\n\n## Why This is the Smallest Booth Game\n\n- No complex rules\n- No inventory or currency\n- No multi-stage turns\n- Just pass object and avoid being last\n- Perfect for quick demo cycles at booth\n\nDeliver: board page, remote MCP server, 4-agent demo script, leaderboard UI. Total implementation time: under 1 week."
